im]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and athena's NOPASSWD sudo policy is tightened so the reviewed [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]approval becomes a real privilege boundary.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]agent_sudo_requests.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/agent_sudo_requests.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-110[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-110/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Sudo manifest contracts and the TTY-attached runner in [/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-runner[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-runner: add the sudo manifest/ledger/risk-badge wire contracts to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase_core and an unprivileged sase_sudo_runner binary (sudo -v, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]per-command sudo -n, sudo -k on the controlling TTY) shipped as a wheel [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]console script.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Typed sudo gate kind with the sase sudo front doors[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]sudo-gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sudo-gate: register the sudo gate kind, add the sase sudo [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]request/answer/list/show CLI group with a questions-style single-turn [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]handoff, requires_tty option enforcement, risk badges, the batch ledger [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]follow-up prompt, and the agent_sudo_requests beta flag.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Ratchet the core pin and dependency floor past the runner [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]surface[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-pin[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-runner[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-pin: ratchet sase-core-revision.txt and the sase-core-rs floor to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the release carrying the sudo runner and bindings, keeping binding [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]validators green.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE review modal and the Authenticate terminal handoff[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]ace-review[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sudo-gate, core-pin[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ace-review: add the 🔐 sudo review modal, the synchronous [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Approve-and-run suspend flow that hands the terminal to the runner, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SUDO/SUDOED statuses, single-active-handoff locking, and completion [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]toasts.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The /sase_sudo generated skill and the raw-sudo PreToolUse [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]guard[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]skill-guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sudo-gate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]skill-guard: author the generated /sase_sudo skill teaching the request [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract, add the chezmoi-managed PreToolUse deny for raw sudo in agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Bash calls, and revise the 'SASE never uses sudo' user-facing copy.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Machine-targeted and remote-raised sudo over ssh -t[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]remote-sudo[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ace-review[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]remote-sudo: add ssh targets to machine records, machine-targeted [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]requests executed over ssh -t with a sealed manifest, remote-raised [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]requests answered via the ssh -t relay from local ACE, and deny-only [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]behavior on every non-TTY surface.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Chezmoi sudo guards and the athena policy tightening[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]athena-policy[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ace-review, skill-guard[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]athena-policy: guard the chezmoi run_onchange scripts against [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]password-required sudo, then live-tighten athena by replacing the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]NOPASSWD:ALL sudoers rule and setting ptrace_scope=1 through the shipped[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]/sase_sudo flow itself.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Canary absence proof, live remote proof, and flag removal[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]acceptance[dim] · [dim][/dim]after remote-sudo, athena-policy[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]acceptance: land the canary-credential absence suite, run the live [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]apollo machine-targeted proof with a real password prompt, remove the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent_sudo_requests flag, and finish docs and polish.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-110","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-110.6","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","wait_for_beads":["sase-110.4"],"workflow_name":"sase-110.6"},"source_run_id":"run-5c1d637de254b09e6f87191ea7fcf260","started_at":"2026-09-15T11:52:59.240774+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,